ENABLE -- the Enhanced North American Benchmark LExicon
======================================================

`enable.txt` in this directory is the widely distributed `enable1.txt` form of the
ENABLE word list: 172,823 entries, lowercase a-z, one per line, LF-terminated,
sorted, committed verbatim and renamed per this repo's one-name rule. Its SHA-256
digest is pinned in `enable.sha256` beside it and every script that reads the file
hashes it and throws on a mismatch.

ENABLE is in the PUBLIC DOMAIN. That is why it is the list this repo uses: it
carries neither an attribution nor a share-alike obligation, unlike the CC BY 4.0
Brysbaert lists anchored at `src/assets/LICENSE-brysbaert`. `package.json`'s
`SEE LICENSE IN LICENSE` is unaffected.

The release statement below is quoted verbatim from the ENABLE2K readme
distributed with the list (the copy read was
https://github.com/BartMassey/wordlists/blob/main/README-enable2k.txt). WORD.LST is
the list's own name for itself; `enable1.txt` and this repo's `enable.txt` are that
file under a distribution name.

